-- ============================================================================
-- Migration 1133: PCB assembly -- the SMT line and through-hole machines (USA, India), the sourced assembly reference, the catalog processes
-- ============================================================================
-- Generated by scripts/generate-pcba-assembly-migration.js; re-run it and diff instead of editing.
--
-- A board with components was priced as a bare board: memory/PCBA covers fabrication only and the PCB catalog had no assembly process.
-- The assembly data was researched and sourced into memory/PCBA/Assembly (user decision 2026-11-23: every row carries its source).
--
-- 1. Machines (mhr_records, process group PCB). 24 machines, each at USA and India rates:
--      Stencil Print           pcba_stencil_printer           2: GKG G5; GKG GT++
--      Solder Paste Inspection pcba_solder_paste_inspection   2: Koh Young KY8030-2; Sinic-Tek B3 in-line 3D SPI
--      Pick and Place          pcba_pick_and_place            1: Yamaha YSM20R
--      Reflow Solder           pcba_reflow                    3: Heller 1809 MK5; JT JTR-800-N; Kait KTE-1000
--      Assembly AOI            pcba_aoi                       3: Koh Young Zenith F 3D AOI; Omron VT-S530 AOI; Sinic-Tek LT-M330D online AOI
--      Wave Solder             pcba_wave_solder               4: Chipbest FMW-350 lead-free dual wave; I.C.T W2 lead-free wave; Jaguar N350 lead-free wave; SFG SH-350 lead-free wave
--      Selective Solder        pcba_selective_solder          3: Sundarc AS-350C selective wave; Sundarc FS-250C desktop selective wave; Sundarc XS-350C dual-pot selective wave
--      In-Circuit Test         pcba_in_circuit_test           1: I.C.T-Q588A online ICT
--      Assembly Flying Probe   pcba_flying_probe              1: I.C.T A40 flying probe
--      Depanel Router          pcba_depanel_router            4: GAM320A router (Kiritsu India); Genitec GAM320 router (Hibex India); I.C.T-5700N offline PCBA router; Indus Robotics PCB depaneling router
--    Rates: the reference's own overhead rule per country, fitted on its PCB machines and reproducing each to the cent (96 USA rows,
--    worst 0.0052; 105 India rows, worst 0.0002 USD/hr), on the machine's price, power and floor area:
--      USA    direct = 6.0535e-5 x price + 0.1511 x kW + 0.0002; indirect = 0.08553 x m² + 13.8333
--      India  direct = 4.8526e-5 x price + 0.1240 x kW + 0.0000; indirect = 0.02910 x m² + 0.8625
--    with the reference's economics (life 10 yr, uptime 80 %, installation 20 %, maintenance 5 %). A machine with no power or size stated has
--    no energy or floor area in its rate (said in its specs).
--    Crew, setup and wage grade: the reference's analogous fabrication machine (memory/PCBA/Machine), its smallest crew:
--      Stencil Print           as Screen Printing                  1 operator(s), setup 0 h (the line changeover), 4 - Metal (USA 43.21, India 2.30 USD/hr)
--      Solder Paste Inspection as Automated Vision Inspection    0.5 operator(s), setup 0 h (the line changeover), 3 - Metal (USA 36.30, India 1.73 USD/hr)
--      Pick and Place          as Drill Circuit Holes              1 operator(s), setup 0 h (the line changeover), 3 - Metal (USA 36.30, India 1.73 USD/hr)
--      Reflow Solder           as Silkscreen Cure                  0 operator(s), setup 0 h (the line changeover), 3 - Metal (USA 36.30, India 1.73 USD/hr)
--      Assembly AOI            as Automated Optical Inspection     1 operator(s), setup 0 h (the line changeover), 3 - Metal (USA 36.30, India 1.73 USD/hr)
--      Wave Solder             as Hot Air Solder Leveling          1 operator(s), setup 0.17 h, 3 - Metal (USA 36.30, India 1.73 USD/hr)
--      Selective Solder        as Hot Air Solder Leveling          1 operator(s), setup 0.17 h, 3 - Metal (USA 36.30, India 1.73 USD/hr)
--      In-Circuit Test         as Bed of Nails                     1 operator(s), setup 0.17 h, 3 - Metal (USA 36.30, India 1.73 USD/hr)
--      Assembly Flying Probe   as Flying Probe                     0 operator(s), setup 0.17 h, 4 - Metal (USA 43.21, India 2.30 USD/hr)
--      Depanel Router          as Router                           1 operator(s), setup 0.25 h, 3 - Metal (USA 36.30, India 1.73 USD/hr)
--    Prices: the new list price; a listing given as a range is one machine at its midpoint (user decision 2026-11-24).
--    Not seeded: used listings (10: Desen DSP-1008 (listing price low); Desen DSP-1008 (listing price high); Parmi HS60L 3D SPI; Juki RS-1R; Juki KE-2080L (listing price low); Juki KE-2080L (listing price high); Yamaha YSM20R (used Alibaba listing); Hanwha SM482 Plus; Pillarhouse Jade S-200 MKII (used 2009, refurbished 2022); Teradyne Spectrum 9 TSE 8862 (used 2006));
--      no price (10: Yamaha YSM10; Ersa HOTFLOW ONE 14; Ersa HOTFLOW THREE 20; BTU Pyramax 100N; BTU Pyramax 125N; I.C.T-Q518D ICT; SPEA 4060 S2 flying probe; SPEA 4050 S2 flying probe; Winsmart SMTR09 router; GAM 340AT in-line automatic PCB router (NewPages listing));
--      loaders and conveyors, which have no process of their own (8).
--    Placers carry their rated and IPC-9850 speed (specs.rated_cph, ipc_cph); reflow ovens their conveyor speed range (specs).
--    THT insertion and hand soldering are bench work on the PCB benches HR Rates holds (pcb_bench_operation, migrations 797 and 1129).
-- 2. The sourced assembly reference, staged whole as lookup tables of source version 2026-PCB (beside migration 1130's):
--      assembly_rates    49 rows (34 keyed)  memory/PCBA/Assembly/assembly_rates.csv: print, SPI and AOI speeds, THT insertion and soldering, test times, depanel speed, line changeover, placement derating
--      assembly_costs    57 rows (14 keyed)  memory/PCBA/Assembly/assembly_costs.csv: stencils, solder paste and its density, the stencil thickness, test fixtures and programs, by region and currency
-- 3. The PCB catalog's assembly processes (process_taxonomy, process_calculator_mappings), each with its machine class; the calculators of
--    migration 1134 activate them.
--
-- Idempotent: a machine already present for its class, location and name is skipped; a staged table is left as it is; a catalog row keeps
-- its machine class and wiring.
-- Verify: SELECT location, machine_class, count(*) FROM mhr_records WHERE machine_class LIKE 'pcba_%' GROUP BY 1, 2 ORDER BY 1, 2;
--   -- expect 24 USA and 24 India rows.
-- ============================================================================

-- specs was dropped by migration 563 and is restored by 814a; added here as
-- well so this file runs on its own. No-op when the column exists.
ALTER TABLE mhr_records ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS specs JSONB;

INSERT INTO mhr_records (
