ycle","value_min":6,"value_max":6,"unit":"s_per_board","conditions":"Yamaha YRP10e printer, core cycle time per sheet; conditions not stated","source_url":"https://global.yamaha-motor.com/business/smt/printer/yrp10e/","source_date":"2026-11-23","source_note":"Manufacturer page: core cycle time of 6.0 seconds per sheet. Datasheet figure."},{"item_key":"print_core_cycle_s","operation":"stencil_print","method":"core_cycle","value_min":12,"value_max":12,"unit":"s_per_board","conditions":"ASMPT DEK TQ XL, large boards up to 850 x 610 mm, up to 8 mm thick, 12 kg","source_url":"https://www.asmpt.com/en/innovation/high-precision-smt-printing/","source_date":"2026-11-23","source_note":"Manufacturer page: core cycle time of 12 seconds. Datasheet figure."},{"item_key":null,"operation":"stencil_print","method":"full_cycle","value_min":22.4,"value_max":22.4,"unit":"s_per_board","conditions":"ASMPT DEK TQ XL, large boards up to 850 x 610 mm","source_url":"https://www.asmpt.com/en/innovation/high-precision-smt-printing/","source_date":"2026-11-23","source_note":"Manufacturer page: full cycle time of 22.4 seconds. Datasheet figure."},{"item_key":"ict_s_at_500_nets","operation":"ict_test","method":"bed_of_nails","value_min":2,"value_max":5,"unit":"s_per_board","conditions":"Bed-of-nails ICT, 500 nets","source_url":"https://www.electronicdesign.com/home/article/21200545/default.asp","source_date":"2000-11-01","source_note":"3,000 nets = 15 to 60 s [moved from assembly_costs.csv at merge]"},{"item_key":"ict_s_at_3000_nets","operation":"ict_test","method":"bed_of_nails","value_min":15,"value_max":60,"unit":"s_per_board","conditions":"Bed-of-nails ICT, 3000 nets","source_url":"https://www.electronicdesign.com/home/article/21200545/default.asp","source_date":"2000-11-01","source_note":"[moved from assembly_costs.csv at merge]"},{"item_key":"assembly_fp_min_at_500_nets","operation":"flying_probe_test","method":"flying_probe","value_min":2,"value_max":5,"unit":"min_per_board","conditions":"Flying probe, 500 nets","source_url":"https://www.electronicdesign.com/home/article/21200545/default.asp","source_date":"2000-11-01","source_note":"3,000 nets = 15 to 60 min [moved from assembly_costs.csv at merge]"},{"item_key":"assembly_fp_min_at_3000_nets","operation":"flying_probe_test","method":"flying_probe","value_min":15,"value_max":60,"unit":"min_per_board","conditions":"Flying probe, 3000 nets","source_url":"https://www.electronicdesign.com/home/article/21200545/default.asp","source_date":"2000-11-01","source_note":"[moved from assembly_costs.csv at merge]"},{"item_key":null,"operation":"ict_test","method":"bed_of_nails","value_min":30,"value_max":30,"unit":"s_per_board","conditions":"Cost-model assumption, including handling time, for both a traditional and a low-cost in-circuit tester","source_url":"https://iconnect007.com//article/45813/optimizing-test-operations-to-cut-costs/45816/smt","source_date":"2026-11-23","source_note":"John VanNewkirk (CheckSum), I-Connect007: \"Assume that both testers take 30 seconds (including handling time) to test a single board\". Article date not shown on the page (placeholder date). An assumption in a worked example, not a measurement."},{"item_key":null,"operation":"conformal_coat","method":"selective_curtain_nozzle","value_min":300,"value_max":800,"unit":"mm_per_s","conditions":"Rehm Protecto selective coater with VarioFlex curtain nozzle; \"typical process speeds\"","source_url":"https://iconnect007.com/article/101335/rehm-develops-new-curtain-nozzle-for-highly-selective-conformal-coating/101338/smt","source_date":"2016-11-29","source_note":"Manufacturer news release in I-Connect007: \"typical process speeds of 300-800 mm/s can be achieved\". Process (applicator travel) speed, not boards per hour."},{"item_key":"depanel_router_mm_per_s","operation":"depanel_router","method":"router_bit","value_min":1,"value_max":100,"unit":"mm_per_s","conditions":"GAM 340AT in-line automatic PCB router: cutting speed \"1-100mm/s (Adjustable)\"; XY move 1000 mm/s, Z 800 mm/s; spindle max 60000 rpm","source_url":"https://www.newpages.asia/my/en/product/4368779/gam-340at-in-line-automatic-pcb-router-machine","source_date":"2026-11-23","source_note":"Reseller listing (Malaysia). Machine setting range, not a recommended feed for a given board thickness or bit. Same 1-100 mm/s range appears on the GAM320A and GAM380AT listings and on an IndiaMART listing for GAM320AT/330AT/340AT/360AT."},{"item_key":"line_changeover_fixed_min","operation":"line_changeover","method":"conventional","value_min":45,"value_max":45,"unit":"min","conditions":"fixed part of one SMT side changeover (old method: manual buddy-system verification against the setup sheet)","source_url":"https://escholarship.org/content/qt0f94x554/qt0f94x554.pdf?t=lnq07f","source_date":"2026-11-23","source_note":"Trovinger & Bohn, Production and Operations Management 14(2), 2005: measured time-study regression setup min = 45 + 1.67 x feeders (old method). Same source as line_changeover.csv."},{"item_key":"feeder_load_min","operation":"line_changeover","method":"conventional","value_min":1.67,"value_max":1.67,"unit":"min_per_feeder","conditions":"incremental setup time per feeder, old method","source_url":"https://escholarship.org/content/qt0f94x554/qt0f94x554.pdf?t=lnq07f","source_date":"2026-11-23","source_note":"Trovinger & Bohn 2005: the regression's slope, 1.67 min per feeder (the conclusion rounds it to 1.7). The SMED + barcode method measured 18 + 0.18 x feeders."},{"item_key":"smt_line_placers","operation":"smt_line","method":"placers_in_series","value_min":1,"value_max":1,"unit":"placement_machines","conditions":"Automotive SMT line 1 (printer, pick-and-place, reflow, AOI), monthly average before SMED (January 2025): one pick-and-place machine","source_url":"https://epubl.ktu.edu/object/elaba:236317136/236317136.pdf","source_date":"2026-11-23","source_note":"The line configuration of the changeover study. Stupelis, Kaunas University of Technology MSc thesis 2025: average 14 min 10 s (90 changeovers, ERP-recorded). Seconds converted to minutes. Measured."},{"item_key":"smt_line_placers","operation":"smt_line","method":"placers_in_series","value_min":2,"value_max":2,"unit":"placement_machines","conditions":"High-mix low-volume line (printer, 2 Universal placement machines, reflow), after improvements, fully hot-swappable products: two placement machines","source_url":"https://etd.auburn.edu/bitstream/handle/10415/2645/SMT%20Line%20Improvements%20for%20High%20Mix,%20Low%20Volume%20Electronics%20Manufacturing%20William%20Swaim.pdf.txt?sequence=3&isAllowed=y","source_date":"2011-08-06","source_note":"The line configuration of the changeover study. Swaim, Auburn thesis: average downtime during setup of completely hot-swappable products 22 min (SD 2.16 min, 4 test runs). Measured."},{"item_key":"smt_line_placers","operation":"smt_line","method":"placers_in_series","value_min":2,"value_max":2,"unit":"placement_machines","conditions":"ASM line (DEK Horizon printer, Siplace TX2 + TX1, Rehm reflow), before rolling pre-kitted feeder carts: two placement machines (TX2 + TX1)","source_url":"https://www.manufacturingtomorrow.com/news/2025/11/03/asm-smt-line-vs-panasonic-npm-real-shop-changeover-and-uptime-data-from-the-floor/26426/","source_date":"2025-11-04","source_note":"The line configuration of the changeover study. Trade press shop-floor report (no named author; links to an SMT line reseller): old changeover averaged 42 min."},{"item_key":"smt_line_placers","operation":"smt_line","method":"placers_in_series","value_min":2,"value_max":2,"unit":"placement_machines","conditions":"Eastern European EMS flexible line (2 placement machines, 10-zone reflow, 3D AOI), before intelligent feeder carts and offline preparation: two placement machines","source_url":"https://smtmachineline.com/building-a-flexible-smt-production-line-from-planning-to-implementation/","source_date":"2026-03-21","source_note":"The line configuration of the changeover study. SMT line supplier blog case study: changeover reduced from 90 minutes average."},{"item_key":"smt_line_placers","operation":"smt_line","method":"placers_in_series","value_min":3,"value_max":3,"unit":"placement_machines","conditions":"5 SMT lines (15 placement machines), offline pre-loaded feeder trolleys plus common setups, high-mix Kanban batches: 15 placement machines on 5 lines: 3 a line","source_url":"https://www.electronics.org/system/files/technical_resource/E6&S30_02.pdf","source_date":"2011-03-29","source_note":"The line configuration of the changeover study. Moffat, IPC APEX paper (PDF created 2011-03-29): average changeover within 5 minutes, measured last PCB of product A to first PCB of product B; 6-8 changeovers per line per 8-h shift; 60 offline pre-loaded trolleys."},{"item_key":"smt_line_placers","operation":"smt_line","method":"placers_in_series","value_min":3,"value_max":3,"unit":"placement_machines","conditions":"3-module placement line, 5,120 mm long, 320 unique feeders, all-manual changeover: three placement modules","source_url":"https://www.circuitnet.com/news/uploads/2/Hitachi_Technical_Feature_Article_Circuitnet_White_Paper.pdf","source_date":"2026-11-23","source_note":"The line configuration of the changeover study. Hitachi High Technologies white paper (Wyglendowski), undated: typical all-manual changeover \"can be more than three quarters of an hour\"; 45 is a lower bound. Feeder cart changeover (2 carts per module) is 2/3 of the downtime. Vendor figure."},{"item_key":"placement_actual_pct_of_ipc","operation":"placement_derating","method":"actual_speed_vs_ipc9850_speed","value_min":60,"value_max":60,"unit":"pct_of_ipc9850","conditions":"Rule of thumb quoted verbatim: \"actual speed is 60% of IPC speed, which is 60% of maximum speed\"; author notes neither figure is clearly defined.","source_url":"https://iconnect007.com/article/80564/smt-trends-and-technologies-what-is-your-real-output/80567/smt","source_date":"2014-04-02","source_note":"Eric Klaver, SMT Magazine column (March 2014 issue); generic, not machine-specific"},{"item_key":"placement_ipc_pct_of_max","operation":"placement_derating","method":"ipc9850_speed_vs_max_rated_speed","value_min":60,"value_max":60,"unit":"pct_of_max_rated","conditions":"Same rule of thumb: IPC speed is 60% of maximum speed. IPC-9850 measured by placing e.g. 80 SOIC-16 or 400 identical 0603 capacitors on a 200 x 200 mm substrate.","source_url":"https://iconnect007.com/article/80564/smt-trends-and-technologies-what-is-your-real-output/80567/smt","source_date":"2014-04-02","source_note":"Eric Klaver, SMT Magazine column; generic"},{"item_key":null,"operation":"placement_derating","method":"actual_throughput_vs_specified_rate","value_min":20,"value_max":40,"unit":"pct_of_rated","conditions":"Phil Zarrow: \"typical machine through-put rates running 20% to 40% of what was originally specified\"","source_url":"https://www.circuitnet.com/board-talk/50504.html","source_date":"2026-11-23","source_note":"Board Talk (Phil Zarrow and Jim Hall, ITM Consulting); episode date not shown, read date used"},{"item_key":null,"operation":"placement_derating","method":"actual_throughput_vs_capacity_good_level","value_min":25,"value_max":25,"unit":"pct_of_capacity","conditions":"Jim Hall: \"if you can get above 25%, that's very good\"; \"you're actually only going to get 25 percent of the machine's capacity\". Threshold only, no max.","source_url":"https://www.circuitnet.com/board-talk/50504.html","source_date":"2026-11-23","source_note":"Board Talk (ITM Consulting); episode date not shown, read date used"},{"item_key":null,"operation":"placement_derating","method":"gap_ipc9850_vs_real_world_europlacer","value_min":15,"value_max":20,"unit":"pct_gap_ipc9850_to_real","conditions":"Chris Merow (Europlacer USA): \"Europlacer, whose IPC rate is within 15-20% of real world production rates\" - vendor claim for Europlacer machines.","source_url":"https://www.circuitnet.com/board-talk/50504.html","source_date":"2015-03-30","source_note":"reader comment on Board Talk page dated Mar 30 2015; vendor self-claim"},{"item_key":null,"operation":"placement_derating","method":"time_at_stated_ipc_rate","value_min":5,"value_max":5,"unit":"pct_of_time","conditions":"Chris Merow: machines \"are running at their stated IPC rate only 5% of the time\"; also \"only about 5% of a real program allows for gang picking\".","source_url":"https://www.circuitnet.com/board-talk/50504.html","source_date":"2015-03-30","source_note":"reader comment on Board Talk page dated Mar 30 2015"}]}$jsonb$::jsonb),
